"""The brAInny ASCII banner — a colored braille render of assets/logo.jpg
via ascii-image-converter (https://github.com/TheZoraiz/ascii-image-converter,
`ascii-image-converter assets/logo.jpg -C -b -H 26`), then quantized
(24-step per RGB channel) and run-length-encoded by hand to shrink the
baked-in size — the raw tool output re-emits a fresh escape+reset for
every single character, which is enormous once the image has any color
variation at all. _GLYPH_COLOR is the ANSI art (truecolor codes, one
reset per run of same-colored characters); _GLYPH_PLAIN is the same
render with color stripped, used verbatim for the no-color path (this
particular art still reads fine in plain braille dots, unlike the old
outline-trace assci.txt approach it replaced).

Shown on bare `brainny` / `brainny --help`. Color is skipped for non-TTY
output or when NO_COLOR is set, per https://no-color.org.

Regenerating: if assets/logo.jpg changes, both constants below must be
regenerated by hand with the command above plus the quantize+RLE pass —
neither is read from the image at runtime.
"""


